Context
  Asked to push the screenshots for review with the flow and the contract and
  integration points.

Deviations
  Three captures were taken; two shipped. The third was a 7KB blank frame from a
  capture taken before Emacs had drawn, and a blank image presented as a trace would
  have been worse than no image. The trace evidence ships as the transcript excerpt
  instead, which is what actually demonstrates it.

Considerations
  I spent a long time trying to photograph ,trace inside Geiser and did not get it.
  The repeated cause was my own polling: loops that test a fast condition complete in
  microseconds, so I captured before Emacs had started, three separate times. The
  working pattern is to poll something that costs real time, and it is written into
  the geiser-setup agent.

  ImageMagick on this cell has no X11 delegate -- import cannot capture and cannot
  decode xwd -- so ffmpeg -f x11grab is the only screenshot path that works here.
  That contradicts the usual 'scrot/import' advice and is worth knowing on FreeBSD.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, guile-sicp, Xvfb :99, GNU Emacs 30.2, ffmpeg x11grab.
